#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4fc3ba4-d488-5156-88dc-837369269cef" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "9199806a-56d9-516c-b5c9-c3a184f8a0be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220637} {:answer-field/id #uuid "bfd89e18-df1a-52e5-b1a9-13b9a350e74e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220638} {:answer-field/id #uuid "1d46c25a-b0e5-5cb8-b4d9-bcfcbeae85f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220639} {:answer-field/id #uuid "5c309815-d4c5-5708-9d45-6e7c0e1436e3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220640}] :question/id #uuid "e415201f-e8d7-5cac-99e4-ae2f79b7e01e" :question/math-academy-id "q-333858" :question/problem "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, e^{At} = \\begin{bmatrix}e^{2t} & te^{2t} \\\\ 0 & e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}$\nGiven the matrices $A$ and $e^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{d}{dt}(e^{At})$.\n\n| $\\frac{d}{dt}(e^{At}) =$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370129 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221409 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a118fe4a-cd1f-52f7-aa33-59f5494e4905" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Exponent for a Matrix With Distinct Complex Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7afe076b-ab10-5a6d-92ee-d9bda36095eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7afe076b-ab10-5a6d-92ee-d9bda36095eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370131} :answer-field/id #uuid "8717736e-bf1d-56b9-8978-2ee27ddc1c10" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116b716d-7743-526a-8367-67bb770fa2aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "116b716d-7743-526a-8367-67bb770fa2aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370133} :answer-field/id #uuid "6684d3cf-4512-5e44-a922-9538752b4a1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eace89bb-5f6d-586f-b6ba-d2d1f4b38da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-334633" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\pm \\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\,\\,$ |  | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & -{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\text{i}t) & ={e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}\\cdot \\text{i}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308674 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221410 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fd1d280-c768-5504-892e-a9a1948e1f1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Exponent for a Matrix With Repeated Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cddbd6d-ffb7-5530-be33-109a25cb590f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cddbd6d-ffb7-5530-be33-109a25cb590f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305736} :answer-field/id #uuid "28239443-16fd-5045-bb7b-a3e946af529a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fff644e-a154-526d-b37a-e4f82a475e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fff644e-a154-526d-b37a-e4f82a475e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306218} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cec750e-1b50-5e87-b62d-239edf61a752" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d74b37d0-1ddd-5304-877c-4617a1e8ae03" :question/math-academy-id "q-334735" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $3,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\,\\,$ |  | $1+4t$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $8t$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 8{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(3t) &={e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(3t) &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{3t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n3t{e}^{3t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}(1-3t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-2{e}^{3t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(-2t) \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-{e}^{3t}t+{e}^{3t}(1-3t) \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(1-4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1+4t & -2t \\\\ 8t & 1-4t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4fc3ba4-d488-5156-88dc-837369269cef" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e5577e5-b719-5b3f-b68d-1a75b4f32803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e5577e5-b719-5b3f-b68d-1a75b4f32803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306635} :answer-field/id #uuid "44dfc463-2eed-5b8f-a49b-1a3832e8c840" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0a7c5d9-d376-5bfc-a898-b72ac7a7d83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0a7c5d9-d376-5bfc-a898-b72ac7a7d83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307230} :answer-field/id #uuid "53a80531-ea9b-5f87-832d-76058c53931d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b1ecd54-364c-5cc5-a146-14c0aa79943d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b1ecd54-364c-5cc5-a146-14c0aa79943d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306024} :answer-field/id #uuid "93f4d138-3d8f-5af5-bab0-3f349b34eb48" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c31d763-cb9f-53cb-b3d1-d640d1818379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c31d763-cb9f-53cb-b3d1-d640d1818379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305410} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb057fc7-7654-5c34-bfa6-3eaa85ee1200" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d14a11c3-0a49-5696-a62c-af65df34be1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-335108" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & -5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
